DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN=your-bot-token-here
DISCORD_CHANNEL_ID=123456789012345678
TORN_API_KEY=your-faction-api-key
FACTION_ID=10739

# ── Chain Watch (#783) ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One bearer per faction the bot watches, named after its dashboard slug:
# forge -> CHAIN_WATCH_TOKEN_FORGE. Printed on the dashboard box with
#   node db/chain-watch-token.mjs <slug>
#
# ⚠️ These live here and nowhere else. Never pass a token through a slash
# command — Discord command arguments are visible to the client and land in
# logs, and a tenant bearer in a channel is a leaked credential for that
# faction. `/chain tenant add` deliberately takes no token parameter.
#
# ⚠️ This is NOT the same value as the dashboard's FLEET_METRICS_TOKEN. Both
# derive from one fleet secret, but the chain-watch token is scoped so that a
# compromise of this bot does not also expose key-pool depth.
# Role allowed to run the leadership-only /chain commands. Unset means anyone.
#CHAIN_LEAD_ROLE_ID=

# ⚠️ Guild ids to sync slash commands to, comma-separated. Set this while
# setting up or demoing: a GLOBAL sync (this unset) is propagated by Discord
# over up to an HOUR, during which the commands are simply absent with no error
# anywhere — an hour spent believing the bot is broken. Guild-scoped is instant.
# Include every server the bot serves, or one of them ends up command-less.
#CHAIN_GUILD_IDS=

#CHAIN_WATCH_TOKEN_FORGE=
#CHAIN_WATCH_TOKEN_TNL=

# Push: let the dashboard tell the bot a board changed, so a sign-up shows up in
# seconds instead of on the next poll. The dashboard container writes to this
# socket over a bind mount.
#
# ⚠️ A socket, not a port: a container cannot reach the host's 127.0.0.1, and
# binding 0.0.0.0 would expose a control channel for this bot to the internet.
#
# ⚠️ Optional and never load-bearing. Unset, or the dashboard not configured,
# means the board updates on its poll interval exactly as before.
# Debounce: /chain set board_debounce_seconds (default 5).
#CHAIN_NOTIFY_SOCKET=/run/chain-notify/notify.sock
